inputs: "INPUTS\n\nObserved light curve (500 epochs, dt~7.2s)\nSatellite mesh (Intelsat 901, ~10k facets)\nEuler dynamics propagator\nConservation laws (T, L constants)\nFFT omega bound" {
  shape: parallelogram
  style.fill: "#D6EAF8"
  style.stroke: "#2980B9"
  style.font-size: 14
}

block1: "BLOCK 1: Select Chain of Consecutive Epochs\n\nChoose 7-10 consecutive epochs with good\nbrightness variation (max range), or brightness-\nseparated epochs with large mag differences (>0.5 mag).\n\nOutput: Chain epoch indices [i1, i2, ... i10]\nwith observed brightness values\n\nTiming: Negligible" {
  class: init
}
n1: "7-10 epochs selected, dt ~ 7.2s" { class: note }

block2: "BLOCK 2: Isobrightness Sampling at Each Epoch\n\nPer epoch: N_SEEDS = 5,000-10,000 random SO(3) seeds.\nL-BFGS-B on brightness-matching objective:\nmin (predicted_B - target_B)^2 over 3 attitude params\n(axis-angle). Lo-fi evaluation. maxiter=50.\nParallelized (8 cores).\n\nOutput per epoch: 50-500 candidate attitudes\nmatching observed brightness within tolerance\n\nTiming: ~20s/epoch x 10 epochs (parallel, 8 cores)" {
  class: optimization
}
n2: "~100 candidates per epoch (50-500 range)\nTotal: ~700-5000 across chain" { class: note }

