block3: "BLOCK 3: Forward Chain - Rotation-Angle Culling\n\nFor each pair (q_j, q_{j+1}):\n  Compute quaternion rotation angle\n  Cull if angle > omega_bound x dt\n  Vectorized: dot-product matrix\n\nLoop over chain links j = 0 to N_CHAIN - 2\n\nKEY: After K links, survival rate\n~ (1 - cull_rate)^K = exponential narrowing\n\nTiming: ~1s per link, ~10s total" {
  class: propagation
}
n3: "~90-99% culled per link\n100x100 = 10,000 pairs -> ~100-1000 survive" { class: note }

block4: "BLOCK 4: Backward Chain - Connectivity Check\n\nPropagate survival constraints backward:\nA candidate at epoch j survives only if\nit has >=1 valid partner at epoch j+1\nthat itself survived the forward pass.\n\nEnsures full-path connectivity through\nALL chain epochs.\n\nOutput: Bidirectionally-filtered candidate sets.\nEach survivor has a valid path through all epochs.\n\nTiming: ~2s (backward sweep)" {
  class: propagation
  style.fill: "#82E0AA"
}
n4: "Survivors further reduced.\nOnly end-to-end valid paths remain." { class: note }

block5: "BLOCK 5: Derive Omega & Consistency Check\n\nFor each pair (q_j, q_{j+1}):\n  omega = rot_vec(q_{j+1} * q_j^-1) / dt\n\nFor triplets: check omega_12 ~ omega_23\nwithin tolerance (0.05 deg/s)\n\nUses KD-tree for efficient spatial matching\nin 3D omega space.\n\nKey filter: ||omega_12 - omega_23|| < threshold\n\nTiming: ~5s (KD-tree build + query)" {
  class: optimization
  style.fill: "#FAD7A0"
}
n5: "~10-50 consistent triplets/paths\nwith derived omega estimates" { class: note }

block6: "BLOCK 6: Energy & Momentum Conservation Filter\n\nFor each candidate with derived omega:\n  T = 0.5 * omega^T * I * omega  (kinetic energy)\n  L = R(q) * (I * omega)  (ang. momentum, inertial)\n\nCheck: T_epoch1 ~ T_epoch2  (within 1%)\nCheck: L_dir_epoch1 ~ L_dir_epoch2  (within 1 deg)\n\nOutput: Physically consistent candidates\nsatisfying torque-free conservation laws\n\nTiming: ~1s" {
  class: propagation
  style.fill: "#76D7C4"
  style.stroke: "#1ABC9C"
}
n6: "0-5 survivors\nPhysics-based post-filter" { class: note }

block7: "BLOCK 7: Propagate & Score Full Light Curve\n\nFor each surviving (q0, omega0):\n  Propagate attitude over full 500-epoch window\n  Generate lo-fi or hi-fi light curve\n  RMS residual vs. observed\n\nOutput: Ranked solution candidates\n\nTiming: ~0.2s/cand (lo-fi) or ~60s/cand (hi-fi)" {
  class: brdf
}

solution: "BEST SOLUTION\n\n(q0, omega0) with lowest RMS residual\n\nSuccess criterion:\nAttitude error < 5 deg\nOmega error < 0.1 deg/s" {
  class: output
}

